UnitStakingRegistry::constants
└── when deployed
    └── it sets _STAKING_REGISTRY_STORAGE_LOCATION to keccak256(abi.encode(uint256(keccak256("geo.storage.StakingRegistry")) - 1)) & ~bytes32(uint256(0xff))

UnitStakingRegistry::constructor
└── when called
    └── it disables initializers

UnitStakingRegistry::initialize
├── when passing valid parameters
│   └── it sets the owner
├── when called twice
│   └── it reverts with InvalidInitialization
└── when council is zero
    └── it reverts with OwnableInvalidOwner

UnitStakingRegistry::setTarget
├── when called by owner
│   ├── it stores the target record
│   └── it emits TargetSet
├── when null type is active
│   └── it reverts with NullTargetCannotBeActive
├── when target id is zero
│   └── it reverts with InvalidTargetId
└── when called by non-owner
    └── it reverts with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount

UnitStakingRegistry::targets
└── when unset
    └── it returns the default record

UnitStakingRegistry::getTargetId
├── when interpreting as a space id
│   └── it matches the space encoding fixtures
├── when interpreting as a topic id
│   └── it folds the high 128 bits for topic ids
└── when fuzzing inputs
    └── it matches the pure derivation rules

UnitStakingRegistry::typeId
└── when called
    └── it returns the type

UnitStakingRegistry::name
└── when called
    └── it returns the name

UnitStakingRegistry::version
└── when called
    └── it returns semantic version

UnitStakingRegistry::_authorizeUpgrade
├── when called by owner
│   └── it authorizes the upgrade
└── when called by non-owner
    └── it reverts with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
